Atlas overlay patch 0040: host/atlas-host-core
Why: the browser must connect to the WolOS bridge (components/atlas_host) when it starts and close the
 connection when it stops, so the downloads menu can offer Share, Open With and Move to Trash only when the
 desktop answers. No lower tier reaches the browser's startup: it is two lines in chrome_browser_main.cc
 (PostBrowserStart, PostMainMessageLoopRun) and an include; the client itself is new files in
 components/atlas_host (the overlay tree), already built into //chrome/browser by patch 0010.
Files: chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
Test filter: *AtlasHost* (components/atlas_host unit tests); journey atlas-reel.yaml step R07
Rebase risk: L (three small hunks near OnBrowserStarted() and web_usb_detector_.reset(), both stable)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in a file the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
@@ -94,6 +94,9 @@
 #include "chrome/common/profiler/thread_profiler_configuration.h"
 #include "chrome/grit/branded_strings.h"
 #include "chrome/installer/util/google_update_settings.h"
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+#include "components/atlas_host/atlas_host.h"
+#endif
 #include "components/color/color_mixers.h"
 #include "components/device_event_log/device_event_log.h"
 #include "components/embedder_support/origin_trials/component_updater_utils.h"
@@ -1733,6 +1736,11 @@
 
   browser_process_->browser_policy_connector()->OnBrowserStarted();
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+  // Atlas: connect to the desktop's bridge (components/atlas_host).
+  atlas_host::AtlasHost::Start();
+#endif
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_PROCESS_SINGLETON)
   // Allow ProcessSingleton to process messages.
   // This is done here instead of just relying on the main message loop's start
@@ -2233,6 +2241,10 @@
 
   web_usb_detector_.reset();
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+  atlas_host::AtlasHost::Stop();
+#endif
+
   for (auto& chrome_extra_part : chrome_extra_parts_) {
     chrome_extra_part->PostMainMessageLoopRun();
   }
